
# Header: <scope>[!]: <subject>
#
# Scope
#
#   - Use a free-form label for the area affected by the change, such as
#     “api”, “cli”, “ui”, “auth”, or “db”.
#   - Append “!” to the scope to signal a breaking change.
#
# Subject
#
#   - Use the imperative mood in the present tense: write “add feature”,
#     not “added feature” or “adds feature”.
#   - Start with a lowercase letter.
#   - Do not end with a period.
#
# Body (optional)
#
#   - Explain what changed and why, not how it was implemented.
#   - Contrast the new behavior with the previous behavior when useful.
#   - May include testing notes, rollback plans, or alternatives considered.
